    <briefdescription>
<para>A <emphasis>classic</emphasis> code example for a <bold>GDExtension</bold> </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The class must inherit from a Godot built in class (like  <godotonly position="open" content="["></godotonly>Object<godotonly position="close" content="]"></godotonly>,  <godotonly position="open" content="["></godotonly>Node<godotonly position="close" content="]"></godotonly>,  <godotonly position="open" content="["></godotonly>Sprite2D<godotonly position="close" content="]"></godotonly>, or  <godotonly position="open" content="["></godotonly>Resource<godotonly position="close" content="]"></godotonly>). Godot does not support multiple inheritance for GDExtension classes.</para>
<para><ref refid="classSummator" kindref="compound">Summator</ref> Example Usage: <programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">var<sp/>sum<sp/>=<sp/>Summator.new()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>sum.add(5)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>sum.add(7)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>var<sp/>total<sp/>=<sp/>sum.get_total()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>#<sp/>prints<sp/>12</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>print(total)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><xrefsect id="signal_1_signal000001"><xreftitle>Signal</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para> <godotonly reference="signal" name="sum_changed(int: sum)"/><parblock><para><bold>sum_changed(int: sum):</bold></para>
<para>This <bold>signal</bold>, is <emphasis>emitted</emphasis> when the sum changes whether after adding a new integer or when resetting the total back to zero.  <godotonly position="open" content="[br][br][b]Note:[/b]"></godotonly>Missing emit signal in total reset function has been recently fixed</para>
</parblock></para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect><simplesect kind="note"><para>Missing emit signal in total reset function has been recently fixed</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<para><xrefsect id="signal_1_signal000002"><xreftitle>Signal</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para> <godotonly reference="signal" name="sum_reset()"/><parblock><para><bold>sum_reset():</bold></para>
<para>This signal is emitted when the total is reset to zero  <godotonly position="open" content="[br][br][b]Note:[/b]"></godotonly>this signal is highly redundant and was added so there would be a warning to parse</para>
</parblock></para>
